<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  The latest released version of each XML Control application.

  Every shipped copy of every app reads this file from
  https://arizona.xml-control.com/versions.xml when the user chooses
  Help > Check for Updates. That address is compiled into the apps, so this file
  must never move or be renamed, and its shape may only change by raising "schema".

  One <release> per major version per channel, holding the latest build in it.
  This is not a history; release notes live on the download page.

    channel   "stable" is read by every copy, licensed or not: an evaluation is the
              same build with no licence. The attribute leaves room for a beta.
    major     point releases within a major are free; a new major is a paid upgrade.
              Must match the first part of version, or apps reject the whole file.
    version   the full four-part build number, compared with System.Version.
    notes     one line, shown in the app's dialog and on the download page.
    page      opened in the browser; apps only open https pages on xml-control.com hosts.
    sha256    optional: the installer's SHA-256, shown on the download page. Apps
              ignore it. Lower-case hex, as certutil -hashfile prints it.

  After editing, run the ControlCircuit test LiveManifest_IsReadable by name: a
  mistake here fails nowhere else, and an app meeting one says it couldn't read the
  update information.

  Design: ControlCircuit/Docs/UpdateCheckerBrief.md
-->
<versions schema="1" updated="2026-09-25">

  <product id="ControlCircuit" name="ControlCircuit">
    <!-- Pre-release placeholder. Replace with the first public build when it ships. -->
    <release channel="stable" major="1" version="1.0.267.0" date="2026-09-25">
      <notes>Pre-release.</notes>
      <page>https://arizona.xml-control.com/controlcircuit/</page>
    </release>
  </product>

</versions>
